<h3>Introduction</h3>
<p>The Include Code macro is an extension wrapper around the Confluence Code macro.
The Confluence Code macro applies syntax highlighting to source code provided as
plain text as the body of the macro.  The Code Include macro has no body, but rather
expects to retrieve the source code from a url.  This is a nice way of keeping source
code examples in the documentation synchronized with the latest version of the code.</p>
<h3>Authentication</h3>
<p>When pulling in the source code from a url, there may be a need to provide a username
and password.  This can be done for each and every macro instance or the Confluence
Admin can configure a default username and password for a given server.</p>
